findings.description:
The plan entry for (152) sets three exit criteria: k-nearest TPS at N=200k within 20% of **k-first** at the same N, parity within 5%, and **no regression on the k-first path**. The design instead:
- removes `k_first` entirely (item 7), which makes two of the three plan criteria unmeasurable;
- adds a new user-facing `radius_only` mode (item 8) that the plan does not assign to this slice;
- re-bases the gate to k-nearest vs `radius_only` (line 358).

Line 55 describes this as "collapsing three `neighbor_mode` values to two", but it is a breaking config change that reaches `ComputeConfig` in the production server from slice 146. The rationale is argued, but the plan entry is not updated and line 34 does not acknowledge that it overrides the plan.

Either amend the plan entry for (152) alongside this design, or keep `k_first` for this slice and move its removal and `radius_only` to a follow-up.
